# Agent Team Host [SPEC:CXC-ATH] — PARKED STUB

> **Parked 2026-07-21 by David.** He was "extremely tempted to run ahead and build the agent
> object/instantiation harness," and deliberately held: the prerequisite is nailing down every element that
> makes an agent's BOOTSTRAP as rich as possible (so it wakes with rich context), because a team host that
> instantiates context-poor members is the wrong thing built well. This file exists so the idea is captured
> in the spec corpus (not only the decision graph) and does not evaporate — it is a skeleton to be filled
> when the bootstrap-richness work (the console config surface: [DEC-PREFS-META-OBJECT-VIEWER] +
> [DEC-DELEGATE-ROLES-ROSTER]) is settled.

---

## 1. Intent (the shape, not the build)

### [CXC-ATH-INTENT] The console is an agent HOST, not a passive viewer

- definition: the console spawns and supervises a TEAM of scoped agents internally. Each member is a
  `(model, profile, brief)` tuple. Members may share a profile with different models (a render-engineer on
  Fable AND on Opus — depth + breadth in parallel) or differ by profile for role sub-specialization (e.g. a
  game-mechanics-specialist alongside a render-engineer for the BSG DRADIS game). Profiles are a PALETTE; a
  team is COMPOSED per task. The host special-cases NO role.
- why parked: the members (and, ultimately, the architect the host will eventually run) must wake with RICH
  context. That richness is defined by the meta-object and its bootstrap manifest — which is the config-surface
  work David chose to settle FIRST. See §4.

## 2. Reuse (do not reinvent when this un-parks)

- **launcher PTY + actuation** (`intelligence/launcher/launcher.py`, [CXC-IC-LIFECYCLE]): a member is a scoped
  `claude` child; the architect is just the persistent, interactive one. Reuse the spawn + 3-phase inject +
  the resume/move re-host wholesale.
- **the subagent-chip UI** (`intelligence_card.py` chips): N hosted members = N chips. The team render surface
  is already built.
- **the bus/peer model**: each member is a peer with its own `intelligence/<member>/{in,out}` namespaces; the
  team is a set of peers on the bus. Same message-passing SHAPE as today's Agent-tool + SendMessage dispatch,
  moved from the harness transport onto PTY-writes over the bus — "collapse the transport, not the seam."

## 3. The genuinely NEW pieces (what slice-1 must build)

- per-member lifecycle in ONE supervisor (spawn / kill / status over a SET, not the singleton the launcher is).
- **deliverable collection**: today the launcher only RELAYS a live interactive session; a scoped member needs
  a terminal "here is my final text, I am done" signal (the harness gives the architect this via the Agent-tool
  completion notification; the console-hosted equivalent is unbuilt).
- brief delivery: a bus namespace or file per member.
- slice-1 = the console hosts ONE ephemeral render-engineer build end-to-end (spawn → brief → activity chips →
  deliverable). Then generalize to a heterogeneous team. Then the architect becomes a persistent+interactive+
  self-compacting member = the full CXC-TWO-APP-CONSOLIDATION.

## 4. Blocking prerequisite (why this is parked, not scheduled)

The member/architect bootstrap must be RICH. That richness lives in the meta-object and the config surface that
views/tunes it — NOT here. Settle those FIRST:
- [DEC-PREFS-META-OBJECT-VIEWER] — the console config surface as a viewer/editor of the meta-object elements
  (identity / dusk gifts / channel / lifecycle threshold / delegate roles), extending the existing
  `registered_checklist` widget family.
- [DEC-DELEGATE-ROLES-ROSTER] — the Intelligence-owned `delegate_roles` on the meta-object (name → role-def
  path + model + why); role-aware dispatch resolves a name to a profile. THIS is where the team's member
  palette actually comes from — the reason the two are coupled.
- the bootstrap manifest itself (`intelligence/launcher/build_bootstrap_prompt` + `intelligence/meta/*.meta.json`):
  what a cold member reads to wake rich.

When those are nailed down, this stub gets filled and slice-1 gets a build order. Until then: PARKED.

